# Large binary assets — project data, not source (~215 MB)
samples/
Issues examples/

# Vendored third-party reference copies (wt-tools, Dagor Asset Explorer),
# including their prebuilt .dll / .exe blobs
reference/

# RAD's Oodle blob. CLAUDE.md §0.2: compiled from Unreal Engine SDK source, governed by the UE
# EULA, for the owner's own install only. It was tracked until 2026-08-25 — harmlessly, since this
# repo has no remote — but no build except the `--rad` diagnostic uses it (the default carries
# the project's own decoder, codecs/wtlz.js), so there is nothing left to weigh against getting it
# out of every future commit.
#
# The history that carried it is gone: the repository was reset to a single root commit on
# 2026-08-25 and `tools/t46_wtlz.mjs` now scans every git object over 100 KB for the RAD bytes on
# every `npm test`, so committing a RAD-built artifact fails the suite instead of going unnoticed.
# docs/LICENSING.md has the whole account. Everything builds and every test passes without this
# file present — it is only needed for `npm run build:rad`, the local A/B diagnostic.
src/vendor/oodle-b64.js

# Scratch and build output
# dist/ holds the diagnostic builds (npm run build:rad, build:ooz-page, build:nooodle) and the
# CDN-loading page (build:cdn) — one of them carries RAD's blob, so keeping dist/ untracked is one
# more thing between that blob and a public repo.
scratchpad/
dist/
# Renamed copies of a build left in the repo root. The tracked artifact is wt_skin_studio.html and
# it IS the release build; another copy is duplicate churn, and this is a repository that
# specifically has to keep large blobs OUT of its history (docs/LICENSING.md).
/wt_skin_studio?*.html
tools/_*.html
tools/_*.mjs
node_modules/
*.wtproj
# ...except the stored project the format test reads (tools/t57_groups.mjs, case 20). It is
# synthetic — no assets/ folder, nothing from the game — which is the only kind that may be tracked.
!tools/fixtures/*.wtproj
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.dll
*.exe
*.wasm
*.obj

